  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="74d3dc49-efae-571d-aeda-0906607d8693" activityNameId="c768497b-c149-5eb1-ab5b-797307b0a6f7" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Door leaf, room, inner, wood-glass, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Door leaf, room, inner, wood-glass, at plant
The measures of the visible door leaf are 0.9m x 2m. The size of the glass insert for the door leaf is 0.7m2. 1m2 of visible glass-wood door leaf weighs 31kg. The bill of materials is based on data from door manufactures.;
UUID: 904295fc-cc1c-3e70-ad9d-442d2c1bd03b
Included are the materials used in an inner room glass-wood door leaf (without surface treatment). Production losses, work materials, packaging materials, energy demand and the transport of the materials are also included.
Location: Data apply to the supply in Switzerland.
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at 4 door manufactures in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_904295fc-cc1c-3e70-ad9d-442d2c1bd03b.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="fdab769f-4bdb-5024-8349-c1745bbb2597" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
